[122.957006, "o", "ETL Transform Fix Summary\r\n=========================\r\n\r\nISSUE:\r\n- CSV export totals were off by 15-20% compared to JSON source\r\n- 41 EUR transactions (€252,897.08) were being skipped\r\n- Script completed without errors but logged warnings\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\n- The parse_amount() function in lib/parsers.py only handled dollar signs ($)\r\n- When processing EUR amounts with € symbol, the regex failed to remove it\r\n- This caused float() conversion to fail, triggering exceptions\r\n- Exceptions were caught and transactions were skipped with warnings logged\r\n\r\nFIX APPLIED:\r\n- Updated lib/parsers.py to handle both $ and € currency symbols\r\n- Changed regex from r'[\\$,]' to r'[\\$€,]'\r\n\r\nVERIFICATION:\r\n- JSON Input: 247 transactions (206 USD + 41 EUR)\r\n- CSV Output: 248 lines (247 data + 1 header) ✓\r\n- USD Total: $1,570,524.26 (matches) ✓\r\n- EUR Total: €252,897.08 (matches) ✓\r\n- No new warnings in logs ✓\r\n\r\nRESULT:\r\n- All transactions now properly exported to CSV\r\n- Amounts accurately reflect source JSON data"]
